<article class="env-definition" id="0FI2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FI2">Definition <span data-tag="0FI2">45.11.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $0$. A <em>Weil cohomology theory</em> over $k$ with coefficients in $F$ is given by data (D0), (D1), (D2), and (D3) satisfying Poincaré duality, the Künneth formula, and compatibility with cycle classes, more precisely, satisfying axioms (A), (B), and (C) of Section <a href="/tag/0FHA" data-tag="0FHA">45.9</a> and in addition such that the equivalent conditions (1) and (2) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0FI0" data-tag="0FI0">45.11.2</a> hold for every smooth projective $X$ over $k$. </p>
</article>